        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Yaşar Kemal, Noam Chomsky\n- Works: Memed, My Hawk\n- Roles: writer, human rights activist, linguist, philosopher, cognitive scientist, historian, social critic, political activist, author\n- Topics: linguistics, war, politics, mass media\n\nFacts:\n- Yaşar Kemal, born Kemal Sadık Gökçeli, was born on 6 October 1923 and died on 28 February 2015.\n- Yaşar Kemal was a Turkish writer and human rights activist of Kurdish origin.\n- Memed, My Hawk, titled İnce Memed in Turkish, is a 1955 novel by Yaşar Kemal.\n- Yaşar Kemal was one of Turkey's leading writers.\n- Noam Chomsky, born Avram Noam Chomsky on 7 December 1928, is an American linguist, philosopher, cognitive scientist, historian, social critic, and political activist.\n- Noam Chomsky is the author of over 100 books on linguistics, war, politics, and mass media.",
